---
title = "How to write a file"
meta_title = "How to write a file in Gleam"
subtitle = "using simplifile"
description = "The simplifile package provides file system functionality that works with Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
---

The `simplifile` package provides file-system functions that work both the
Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add simplifile
```

Use the [`simplfile.write`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#write)
function to write content to a file. If the file does not exist it will be
created, and if it does already exist then the contents will be replaced.

```gleam
import simplifile

pub fn write_greeting() -> Result(Nil, simplifile.FileError) {
  simplifile.write(to: "greeting.txt", contents: "Hello, Joe!\n")
}
```

If you want to write binary data to a file then you can use the
[`simplfile.write_bits`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#write_bits)
function instead.

```gleam
import simplifile

pub fn write_data() -> Result(Nil, simplifile.FileError) {
  simplifile.write_bits("data.bin", <<1, 2, 3, 4, 5>>)
}
```

If the file cannot be written for any reason, these functions will return a
[`simplifile.FileError`](https://simplifile.hexdocs.pm/simplifile.html#FileError).

::: alert-warning
### Files and web browsers

For security reasons web browsers do not let code directly read and write
files, so if your program runs in browser you will need to use a different
approach.

:::
